Subject: Cantor SJS Commit Placement Acquisition P3 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] ce31711a-b797-4327-9321-9438d3ed2b5c
@ [canonical_uuid] 7602b617-05c5-459a-8a78-23bcd638e164

& [Why]
  + P2 deliberately treats placement as supplied data and therefore cannot prove the record exists in Git
  + SWA-05 must not consume supplied placement as physical truth
  + exact commit parent tree path mode blob and canonical bytes are the smallest sufficient physical bridge

& [WhyNow]
  + P0 P1 and P2 are published and their next declared frontier is physical placement observation

& [WhyThisShape]
  + one embedded validated P2 journal preserves semantic continuity
  + raw object reads avoid worktree filters newline conversion and ambient ref ambiguity
  + observation-only receipts prevent evidence from becoming mutation authority

& [WhyNotBroader]
  + hook staging commit push recovery operator policy and provider activation introduce distinct effects and require later signatures
